  "payload_hash": "sha256"
}
```

## Dashboard and alert behavior

The dashboard is the system of record. Telegram is a delivery channel, not a source of truth. Each alert links to its immutable event, source evidence, pattern measurements, option contract quote, score, selected target, structural stop, risk explanation, and status.

The dashboard separately shows Core Paper Alerts and Exploratory Sentiment Alerts. It reports alerts, fills, unfilled orders, expiries, stops, target labels, per lot option P and L, normalized R, sector exposure, data failures, source status, model version, and cohort status.

## Acceptance tests

| Area | Required proof |
| --- | --- |
| Point in time data | No input with `available_at` after `decision_at` reaches a model or report |
| Patterns | All four families and every long short variant have golden fixtures and rejection fixtures |
| Liquidity sweep | Daily or weekly level is present; reversal and continuation variants remain distinct |
| Fills | Buy at ask and sell at bid; gap and both touch fixtures behave by documented policy |
| Options | Contract obeys 7 to 30 DTE and liquidity constraints; premium emergency exit works |
| Vision | Generated point in time charts only; human selected examples cannot enter scored data |
| Sentiment | Every source is approved and every LLM result is attributable and reproducible |
| Validation | Walk forward and embargo tests are enforced; no random split utility is allowed |
| Governance | Change proposal cannot alter an active model without Aditya approval |
| Ledger | Every candidate state reconciles with no silent exclusion or overwritten event |
| Delivery | Dashboard and Telegram payloads reference the same immutable alert |

## Implementation sequence

1. Establish bar availability, source registry, data validation, and immutable ledger.
2. Build underlying pattern engine, higher timeframe liquidity sweep contract, and direction symmetric replay.
3. Add option contract data, bid ask fills, costs, expiry, and settlement.
4. Build walk forward research harness and pattern direction cohort reports.
5. Add raw feature model and calibrated publication rules.
6. Add systematic chart generation and vision model comparison.
7. Add approved sentiment ingestion and separate exploratory stream.
8. Add dashboard, Telegram delivery, approval workflow, and health monitoring.
9. Run immutable forward paper cohorts. Funded execution remains a separate future approval.

